## Authentication

The provider resolves credentials the same way as the LangSmith SDK and CLI:

- **Provider arguments** — `api_key`, `api_url`, `control_plane_url`, `workspace_id`, `profile`.
- **Profile** — set `profile` (or `LANGSMITH_PROFILE`) to select a LangSmith CLI profile.
- **Environment** — `LANGSMITH_API_KEY`, `LANGSMITH_ENDPOINT` (API URL), `LANGSMITH_CONTROL_PLANE_URL`, `LANGSMITH_WORKSPACE_ID`.

Create an API key in your LangSmith workspace settings. Prefer environment or profile
configuration over hardcoding `api_key`; if you set it inline, mark it sensitive and
source it from a secret store.

## Deployment control planes

When `api_url` or `LANGSMITH_ENDPOINT` selects a SaaS region, deployment resources
and revision data sources use that region's control plane by default:

| Region | API URL | Control-plane URL |
| --- | --- | --- |
| GCP US | `https://api.smith.langchain.com` | `https://api.host.langchain.com` |
| GCP EU | `https://eu.api.smith.langchain.com` | `https://eu.api.host.langchain.com` |
| GCP APAC | `https://apac.api.smith.langchain.com` | `https://apac.api.host.langchain.com` |
| AWS US | `https://aws.api.smith.langchain.com` | `https://aws.api.host.langchain.com` |

Set `control_plane_url` or `LANGSMITH_CONTROL_PLANE_URL` to override this default.
When the endpoint comes only from a profile, set the control-plane URL explicitly.

